IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ira-dates`

-- Industrial Relations Act 1996 (NSW) -- the rules a person bringing an employment claim meets: unfair dismissal
-- (Chapter 2 Part 6), public sector disciplinary appeals (Chapter 2 Part 7), unfair contracts (Chapter 2 Part 9
-- Division 2), freedom from victimisation (Chapter 5 Part 1, ss 210 and 213) and the recovery of unpaid remuneration
-- and other amounts (Chapter 7 Part 2). Seat-neutral: the seat layer (ira-seat.l4) asks the questions.
--
-- Every time limit is one regulative rule (the application must be made within the days the Act allows), run by
-- EVALTRACE inside a function that takes only plain facts. Judgments the Act leaves to the Commission are either
-- inputs (where they decide a test) or answered conditionally (where they decide whether a late application is taken).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 2 March 2025). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The time limits: one regulative rule`

DECLARE `Claim party` IS ONE OF `the applicant`
DECLARE `Claim act` IS ONE OF `make the application`

-- ss 85(1), 100B(2), 108B(1), 213(3), 369(3): the application must be made within the time the Act fixes. Day 0 is
-- the day the time runs from (fork F2); the days allowed run to the last day.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim act`
`the application must be made within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    MUST   `make the application`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "the application was not made within the time the Industrial Relations Act 1996 fixes"

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: FULFILLED means made in time.
GIVEN `the clock start` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE, `the day made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`made by the last day` `the clock start` `the last day` `the day made` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the application must be made within` (`the days from` `the clock start` `to` `the last day`)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `make the application` (`the days from` `the clock start` `to` `the day made`)))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The day an application counts as made: the day it was made, or, if it has not been made, today.
GIVEN `it has been made` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day made` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day considered` `it has been made` `the day made` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been made` THEN `the day made` ELSE `today`

§ `Chapter 1: who is an employee (s 5)`

-- s 5(4): "A person employed or engaged by his or her spouse, de facto partner or parent is not an employee".
DECLARE `Who engaged me` IS ONE OF
    `someone other than my spouse, de facto partner or parent`
    `my spouse or de facto partner`
    `my parent`

-- s 5(1): employee "means" (a) a person employed in any industry (whether on salary, wages or piece rates; s 5(2): even
-- on a labour-only contract, part-time or casual, as a lessee of tools, as an outworker, or on commission) or (b) a
-- person Schedule 1 deems an employee. "Employed" is borrowed and asked as a fact.
GIVEN `employed in an industry` IS A BOOLEAN, `deemed by Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN, `engaged by` IS A `Who engaged me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an employee under s 5` `employed in an industry` `deemed by Schedule 1` `engaged by` IF
        (`employed in an industry` OR `deemed by Schedule 1`)
    AND (`engaged by` EQUALS `someone other than my spouse, de facto partner or parent`)

§ `Chapter 2 Part 6: unfair dismissals`

§§ `Whether Part 6 applies (ss 83, 84)`

-- s 83(1)(b): $62,200, "or such greater amount as is prescribed by the regulations". The regulation is not deposited:
-- a figure the person gives is used only where it is greater (finding 2).
GIVEN `a regulation prescribes an amount` IS A BOOLEAN, `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 83 threshold` `a regulation prescribes an amount` `the prescribed amount` MEANS
    IF `a regulation prescribes an amount`
    THEN `the greater of` 62200 `and` `the prescribed amount`
    ELSE 62200

-- s 83(5) "dismissal includes" (a) the threat of dismissal and (b) for a public sector employee, dispensing with the
-- services, dismissal after disciplinary proceedings or an offence, or annulling the appointment.
DECLARE `What happened to me` IS ONE OF
    `I was dismissed`
    `I was threatened with dismissal`
    `my services were dispensed with or my appointment annulled`
    `I was neither dismissed nor threatened with dismissal`

DECLARE `Part 6 answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: Part 6 applies, and you may apply to the Industrial Relations Commission for your claim that the dismissal is harsh, unreasonable or unjust to be dealt with (ss 83, 84(1)); an industrial organisation of employees may apply for you (s 84(2))`
    `no: you are not an employee under this Act, because a person employed or engaged by their spouse, de facto partner or parent is not one (s 5(4))`
    `no: you are not an employee under this Act: an employee means a person employed in an industry, or a person Schedule 1 deems an employee (s 5(1))`
    `no: Part 6 does not apply to the dismissal of an apprentice or trainee (other than an existing worker trainee) (s 83(3))`
    `no: Part 6 does not apply to the dismissal of a Department Secretary, a Public Service senior executive or a police executive officer (s 83(3))`
    `no: Part 6 does not apply to an employee a regulation exempts from it (s 83(2))`
    `no: Part 6 does not apply, because you were employed under a Federal award and can apply (or but for an exclusion could apply) to the Fair Work Commission about this dismissal (s 83(1A))`
    `no: Part 6 does not apply to an employee whose conditions are not set by an industrial instrument and whose annual remuneration is above the threshold (s 83(1)(b))`
    `this Act does not say: dismissal includes dispensing with services and annulling an appointment for a public sector employee (s 83(5)(b)), and is silent for other employees`
    `no: Part 6 deals with a dismissal (including the threat of one), and you were neither dismissed nor threatened (ss 83(5), 84(1))`
    `no: Part 6 deals with an employee's claim that the dismissal is harsh, unreasonable or unjust, and you do not make that claim (s 84(1))`

GIVEN `employed in an industry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deemed by Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `engaged by` IS A `Who engaged me`
      `public sector employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apprentice or trainee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `senior office holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exempted by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employed under a Federal award` IS A BOOLEAN
      `can go to the Fair Work Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conditions set by an industrial instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `annual remuneration` IS A NUMBER
      `a regulation prescribes an amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
      `what happened` IS A `What happened to me`
      `claims harsh, unreasonable or unjust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Part 6 answer`
`the Part 6 answer` `employed in an industry` `deemed by Schedule 1` `engaged by` `public sector employee` `apprentice or trainee` `senior office holder` `exempted by regulation` `employed under a Federal award` `can go to the Fair Work Commission` `conditions set by an industrial instrument` `annual remuneration` `a regulation prescribes an amount` `the prescribed amount` `what happened` `claims harsh, unreasonable or unjust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`engaged by` EQUALS `someone other than my spouse, de facto partner or parent`))
            THEN `no: you are not an employee under this Act, because a person employed or engaged by their spouse, de facto partner or parent is not one (s 5(4))`
        IF (NOT (`is an employee under s 5` `employed in an industry` `deemed by Schedule 1` `engaged by`))
            THEN `no: you are not an employee under this Act: an employee means a person employed in an industry, or a person Schedule 1 deems an employee (s 5(1))`
        IF `apprentice or trainee`
            THEN `no: Part 6 does not apply to the dismissal of an apprentice or trainee (other than an existing worker trainee) (s 83(3))`
        IF `senior office holder`
            THEN `no: Part 6 does not apply to the dismissal of a Department Secretary, a Public Service senior executive or a police executive officer (s 83(3))`
        IF `exempted by regulation`
            THEN `no: Part 6 does not apply to an employee a regulation exempts from it (s 83(2))`
        IF `employed under a Federal award` AND `can go to the Fair Work Commission`
            THEN `no: Part 6 does not apply, because you were employed under a Federal award and can apply (or but for an exclusion could apply) to the Fair Work Commission about this dismissal (s 83(1A))`
        IF (NOT `public sector employee`) AND (NOT `conditions set by an industrial instrument`) AND (`annual remuneration` GREATER THAN `the s 83 threshold` `a regulation prescribes an amount` `the prescribed amount`)
            THEN `no: Part 6 does not apply to an employee whose conditions are not set by an industrial instrument and whose annual remuneration is above the threshold (s 83(1)(b))`
        IF (`what happened` EQUALS `my services were dispensed with or my appointment annulled`) AND (NOT `public sector employee`)
            THEN `this Act does not say: dismissal includes dispensing with services and annulling an appointment for a public sector employee (s 83(5)(b)), and is silent for other employees`
        IF `what happened` EQUALS `I was neither dismissed nor threatened with dismissal`
            THEN `no: Part 6 deals with a dismissal (including the threat of one), and you were neither dismissed nor threatened (ss 83(5), 84(1))`
        IF (NOT `claims harsh, unreasonable or unjust`)
            THEN `no: Part 6 deals with an employee's claim that the dismissal is harsh, unreasonable or unjust, and you do not make that claim (s 84(1))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: Part 6 applies, and you may apply to the Industrial Relations Commission for your claim that the dismissal is harsh, unreasonable or unjust to be dealt with (ss 83, 84(1)); an industrial organisation of employees may apply for you (s 84(2))`

§§ `The time for applying (s 85)`

GIVEN `the day of the dismissal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 85 last day` `the day of the dismissal` MEANS `the day of the dismissal` `plus days` 21

DECLARE `Part 6 time answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the application was made not later than 21 days after the dismissal (s 85(1))`
    `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 21 days after the dismissal have not passed (s 85(1))`
    `out of time, but the Commission must accept it: you made a similar application under Commonwealth law in time, it was not settled or determined, and this application is (or, made today, would be) made within 21 days after that one was withdrawn or declined because of the remedy under Part 6 (s 85(2))`
    `out of time: more than 21 days after the dismissal; the Commission may accept it only if it considers there is a sufficient reason, having regard to the reason for and length of the delay, the hardship to you or the employer, and the employer's conduct (s 85(3))`

GIVEN `the day of the dismissal` IS A DATE
      `it has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day made` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `made a similar Commonwealth application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made within the Commonwealth time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been settled or determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was withdrawn or declined for the Part 6 remedy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was withdrawn or declined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Part 6 time answer`
`the s 85 answer` `the day of the dismissal` `it has been made` `the day made` `today` `made a similar Commonwealth application` `it was made within the Commonwealth time` `it has been settled or determined` `it was withdrawn or declined for the Part 6 remedy` `the day it was withdrawn or declined` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `made by the last day` `the day of the dismissal` (`the s 85 last day` `the day of the dismissal`) `the day` AND `it has been made`
            THEN `in time: the application was made not later than 21 days after the dismissal (s 85(1))`
        IF `made by the last day` `the day of the dismissal` (`the s 85 last day` `the day of the dismissal`) `the day`
            THEN `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 21 days after the dismissal have not passed (s 85(1))`
        IF     `made a similar Commonwealth application`
           AND `it was made within the Commonwealth time`
           AND (NOT `it has been settled or determined`)
           AND `it was withdrawn or declined for the Part 6 remedy`
           AND `made by the last day` `the day it was withdrawn or declined` (`the day it was withdrawn or declined` `plus days` 21) `the day`
            THEN `out of time, but the Commission must accept it: you made a similar application under Commonwealth law in time, it was not settled or determined, and this application is (or, made today, would be) made within 21 days after that one was withdrawn or declined because of the remedy under Part 6 (s 85(2))`
        OTHERWISE `out of time: more than 21 days after the dismissal; the Commission may accept it only if it considers there is a sufficient reason, having regard to the reason for and length of the delay, the hardship to you or the employer, and the employer's conduct (s 85(3))`
    WHERE
        `the day` MEANS `the day considered` `it has been made` `the day made` `today`

§§ `What the Commission may order (ss 84(4), 89, 90)`

-- The Commission's view on reinstatement is a judgment, asked as an input (s 89(2), (5)).
DECLARE `Commission's view on reinstatement` IS ONE OF
    `reinstatement is practicable`
    `reinstatement is impracticable, but re-employment in another suitable position is practicable`
    `reinstatement and re-employment are both impracticable`

DECLARE `Part 6 remedy answer` IS ONE OF
    `reinstatement (s 89(1)), with pay for the time lost of at most` HAS `the most` IS A NUMBER
    `re-employment in another suitable position (s 89(2)), with pay for the time lost of at most` HAS `the most` IS A NUMBER
    `compensation of at most (s 89(5))` HAS `the most` IS A NUMBER
    `no order under s 89: another law gives you redress for the dismissal, and you have started proceedings under it or have not lodged a written undertaking not to proceed under it (s 90)`

-- s 89(5): the cap is the remuneration "during the period of 6 months immediately before being dismissed", with leave
-- without full pay counted as if on full pay: the remuneration received plus the shortfall on such leave.
GIVEN `remuneration in the 6 months` IS A NUMBER, `shortfall on leave without full pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 89(5) cap` `remuneration in the 6 months` `shortfall on leave without full pay` MEANS
    `remuneration in the 6 months` PLUS `shortfall on leave without full pay`

GIVEN `the view` IS A `Commission's view on reinstatement`
      `another law gives redress` IS A BOOLEAN
      `started proceedings under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lodged an undertaking not to proceed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `remuneration in the 6 months` IS A NUMBER
      `shortfall on leave without full pay` IS A NUMBER
      `remuneration lost until reinstatement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Part 6 remedy answer`
`the Part 6 remedy` `the view` `another law gives redress` `started proceedings under it` `lodged an undertaking not to proceed` `remuneration in the 6 months` `shortfall on leave without full pay` `remuneration lost until reinstatement` MEANS
    IF `another law gives redress` AND (`started proceedings under it` OR (NOT `lodged an undertaking not to proceed`))
    THEN `no order under s 89: another law gives you redress for the dismissal, and you have started proceedings under it or have not lodged a written undertaking not to proceed under it (s 90)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the view`
         WHEN `reinstatement is practicable` THEN `reinstatement (s 89(1)), with pay for the time lost of at most` `remuneration lost until reinstatement`
         WHEN `reinstatement is impracticable, but re-employment in another suitable position is practicable` THEN `re-employment in another suitable position (s 89(2)), with pay for the time lost of at most` `remuneration lost until reinstatement`
         WHEN `reinstatement and re-employment are both impracticable` THEN `compensation of at most (s 89(5))` (`the s 89(5) cap` `remuneration in the 6 months` `shortfall on leave without full pay`)

§ `Chapter 2 Part 7: public sector disciplinary appeals`

§§ `Whether I may appeal (ss 91, 92, 97, 98, 99)`

-- s 97(1): the appealable decisions, a closed list ("This section applies to the following decisions").
DECLARE `Employer's decision` IS ONE OF
    `to defer payment of an increment` HAS `months deferred` IS A NUMBER
    `to reduce my rank, classification, position, grade or pay`
    `to impose a fine or forfeit pay`
    `to annul my appointment on probation`
    `to suspend me as a punishment for misconduct or a breach of a law, rule or direction`
    `to dismiss me (including dispensing with my services)`
    `to direct or require me to resign`
    `another decision`

DECLARE `Disciplinary appeal answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may appeal to the Industrial Relations Commission against the decision (s 98(1)), on any ground including that it was a detrimental action offence under the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (s 98(2))`
    `no: Part 7 appeals are for public sector employees (s 91, s 98(1))`
    `no: a deferral of an increment is appealable only if it is for more than 6 months (s 97(1)(a))`
    `no: the decision is not one of the appealable decisions listed in s 97(1)`
    `no: an award, enterprise agreement or other instrument or arrangement excludes your class from appealing to the Commission (s 92(1))`
    `no: an employee engaged for a specified period or task of less than 6 months cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(a))`
    `no: an employee serving a probation or qualifying period fixed in advance at 3 months or less, or at a longer reasonable period, cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(b))`
    `no: an employee engaged on a casual basis for a short period, not regular and systematic for 6 months with a reasonable expectation of continuing, cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(c))`
    `no: you elected in writing to forgo your s 98 appeal against this decision (s 99(2)(a))`
    `no: you have appealed or brought other proceedings about this decision elsewhere, or they were brought for you (s 99(2)(b))`

GIVEN `the decision` IS AN `Employer's decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an annulment, dismissal or direction to resign` `the decision` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `to annul my appointment on probation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to dismiss me (including dispensing with my services)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to direct or require me to resign` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `public sector employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision` IS AN `Employer's decision`
      `excluded by an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `engaged for a specified period or task` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months of the period or task` IS A NUMBER
      `serving probation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `probation fixed in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months of probation` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commission finds the longer probation reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `casual for a short period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regular and systematic for 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable expectation of continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `elected to forgo` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Disciplinary appeal answer`
`the Part 7 answer` `public sector employee` `the decision` `excluded by an instrument` `engaged for a specified period or task` `months of the period or task` `serving probation` `probation fixed in advance` `months of probation` `the Commission finds the longer probation reasonable` `casual for a short period` `regular and systematic for 6 months` `reasonable expectation of continuing` `elected to forgo` `other proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `public sector employee`)
            THEN `no: Part 7 appeals are for public sector employees (s 91, s 98(1))`
        IF `the decision` EQUALS `another decision`
            THEN `no: the decision is not one of the appealable decisions listed in s 97(1)`
        IF `a short deferral`
            THEN `no: a deferral of an increment is appealable only if it is for more than 6 months (s 97(1)(a))`
        IF `excluded by an instrument`
            THEN `no: an award, enterprise agreement or other instrument or arrangement excludes your class from appealing to the Commission (s 92(1))`
        IF `is an annulment, dismissal or direction to resign` `the decision` AND `engaged for a specified period or task` AND (`months of the period or task` LESS THAN 6)
            THEN `no: an employee engaged for a specified period or task of less than 6 months cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(a))`
        IF `is an annulment, dismissal or direction to resign` `the decision` AND `serving probation` AND `probation fixed in advance` AND ((`months of probation` AT MOST 3) OR `the Commission finds the longer probation reasonable`)
            THEN `no: an employee serving a probation or qualifying period fixed in advance at 3 months or less, or at a longer reasonable period, cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(b))`
        IF `is an annulment, dismissal or direction to resign` `the decision` AND `casual for a short period` AND (NOT (`regular and systematic for 6 months` AND `reasonable expectation of continuing`))
            THEN `no: an employee engaged on a casual basis for a short period, not regular and systematic for 6 months with a reasonable expectation of continuing, cannot appeal against annulment, dismissal or a direction to resign (s 98(3)(c))`
        IF `elected to forgo`
            THEN `no: you elected in writing to forgo your s 98 appeal against this decision (s 99(2)(a))`
        IF `other proceedings`
            THEN `no: you have appealed or brought other proceedings about this decision elsewhere, or they were brought for you (s 99(2)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you may appeal to the Industrial Relations Commission against the decision (s 98(1)), on any ground including that it was a detrimental action offence under the Public Interest Disclosures Act 2022 (s 98(2))`
    WHERE
        `a short deferral` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the decision`
            WHEN `to defer payment of an increment` m THEN m AT MOST 6
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `The time for appealing (s 100B)`

GIVEN `the day I was notified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 100B last day` `the day I was notified` MEANS `the day I was notified` `plus days` 28

DECLARE `Disciplinary appeal time answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the notice of appeal was lodged within 28 days after you were notified of the decision (s 100B(2))`
    `still in time: you have not lodged a notice of appeal yet, and 28 days after you were notified of the decision have not passed (s 100B(2))`
    `out of time: a notice of appeal must be lodged within 28 days after you are notified of the decision (s 100B(2)), and Part 7 gives the Commission no power to accept a late one`

GIVEN `the day I was notified` IS A DATE, `it has been made` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day made` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Disciplinary appeal time answer`
`the s 100B answer` `the day I was notified` `it has been made` `the day made` `today` MEANS
    IF `made by the last day` `the day I was notified` (`the s 100B last day` `the day I was notified`) (`the day considered` `it has been made` `the day made` `today`)
    THEN IF `it has been made`
         THEN `in time: the notice of appeal was lodged within 28 days after you were notified of the decision (s 100B(2))`
         ELSE `still in time: you have not lodged a notice of appeal yet, and 28 days after you were notified of the decision have not passed (s 100B(2))`
    ELSE `out of time: a notice of appeal must be lodged within 28 days after you are notified of the decision (s 100B(2)), and Part 7 gives the Commission no power to accept a late one`

§ `Chapter 2 Part 9 Division 2: unfair contracts`

§§ `Whether the contract is an unfair contract (s 105)`

DECLARE `Unfair contract answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: an industrial instrument is not a contract for Part 9 (s 105(1))`
    `yes: the contract is unfair, harsh or unconscionable (s 105(1)(a))`
    `yes: the contract is against the public interest (s 105(1)(b))`
    `yes: the contract provides a total remuneration less than an employee performing the work would receive (s 105(1)(c))`
    `yes: the contract is designed to avoid, or does avoid, the provisions of an industrial instrument (s 105(1)(d))`
    `no: an unfair contract means one that is unfair, harsh or unconscionable, against the public interest, underpays against an employee doing the work, or avoids an industrial instrument, and on these facts the contract is none of them (s 105(1))`

-- s 105(1) "unfair contract means": a closed definition. (a), (b) and (d) are the Commission's findings, asked as
-- inputs; (c) is worked out from the two amounts.
GIVEN `it is an industrial instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission finds it unfair, harsh or unconscionable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission finds it against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `total remuneration under the contract` IS A NUMBER
      `what an employee doing the work would receive` IS A NUMBER
      `it is designed to avoid or avoids an industrial instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Unfair contract answer`
`the s 105 answer` `it is an industrial instrument` `the Commission finds it unfair, harsh or unconscionable` `the Commission finds it against the public interest` `total remuneration under the contract` `what an employee doing the work would receive` `it is designed to avoid or avoids an industrial instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an industrial instrument`
            THEN `no: an industrial instrument is not a contract for Part 9 (s 105(1))`
        IF `the Commission finds it unfair, harsh or unconscionable`
            THEN `yes: the contract is unfair, harsh or unconscionable (s 105(1)(a))`
        IF `the Commission finds it against the public interest`
            THEN `yes: the contract is against the public interest (s 105(1)(b))`
        IF `total remuneration under the contract` LESS THAN `what an employee doing the work would receive`
            THEN `yes: the contract provides a total remuneration less than an employee performing the work would receive (s 105(1)(c))`
        IF `it is designed to avoid or avoids an industrial instrument`
            THEN `yes: the contract is designed to avoid, or does avoid, the provisions of an industrial instrument (s 105(1)(d))`
        OTHERWISE `no: an unfair contract means one that is unfair, harsh or unconscionable, against the public interest, underpays against an employee doing the work, or avoids an industrial instrument, and on these facts the contract is none of them (s 105(1))`

§§ `Whether I may apply (ss 106, 108, 108A, 109A)`

DECLARE `My place in the contract` IS ONE OF
    `I am a party to the contract`
    `I would be a party to the contract but for an order`
    `I am not a party to the contract`

DECLARE `Unfair contract application answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may apply to the Commission in Court Session for an order declaring the contract wholly or partly void, or varying it (ss 106, 108)`
    `no: only a party (or would-be party), or the industrial organisations and associations s 108 names, may apply (s 108, "and not otherwise")`
    `no: an industrial instrument is not a contract for Part 9 (s 105(1))`
    `no: the order is for a contract whereby a person performs work in an industry, or a related condition or collateral arrangement where the work is a significant purpose of the arrangements (s 106(1), (2A))`
    `no: Division 2 does not apply where the contract of employment is said to be unfair for a reason for which an unfair dismissal application has been or could have been made under Part 6, or could have been but for s 83 (s 109A)`
    `no: no application can be made about a contract of employment whose remuneration package over the 12 months before the application (or the termination) exceeds the remuneration cap (s 108A(1))`
    `no: a partner cannot apply about a contract with the other partners if the partner's profit share over the 12 months before the application (or the termination) exceeds the cap (s 108A(2))`

-- s 108A(3) remuneration cap: $200,000, or "any greater amount prescribed by the regulations". The regulation is not
-- deposited: a figure the person gives is used only where it is greater (finding 2). s 108A(2)(b)(ii) uses "that
-- amount" if one is prescribed for para (b) of the cap; the same figure is used.
GIVEN `a regulation prescribes a cap` IS A BOOLEAN, `the prescribed cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the remuneration cap` `a regulation prescribes a cap` `the prescribed cap` MEANS
    IF `a regulation prescribes a cap`
    THEN `the greater of` 200000 `and` `the prescribed cap`
    ELSE 200000

-- s 108A(1)(b): a package paid over less than 12 months is taken over 12 months (fork F5: pro rata by months).
GIVEN `the package` IS A NUMBER, `months it covers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the package over 12 months` `the package` `months it covers` MEANS
    IF `months it covers` AT LEAST 12
    THEN `the package`
    ELSE (`the package` TIMES 12) DIVIDED BY `months it covers`

GIVEN `my place` IS A `My place in the contract`
      `it is an industrial instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I perform work in an industry under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is related or collateral to such a contract with work a significant purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason is one for an unfair dismissal application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `remuneration package` IS A NUMBER
      `months the package covers` IS A NUMBER
      `I am a partner and it is with my partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `profit share` IS A NUMBER
      `a regulation prescribes a cap` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Unfair contract application answer`
`the unfair contract application answer` `my place` `it is an industrial instrument` `I perform work in an industry under it` `it is related or collateral to such a contract with work a significant purpose` `it is a contract of employment` `the reason is one for an unfair dismissal application` `remuneration package` `months the package covers` `I am a partner and it is with my partners` `profit share` `a regulation prescribes a cap` `the prescribed cap` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `my place` EQUALS `I am not a party to the contract`
            THEN `no: only a party (or would-be party), or the industrial organisations and associations s 108 names, may apply (s 108, "and not otherwise")`
        IF `it is an industrial instrument`
            THEN `no: an industrial instrument is not a contract for Part 9 (s 105(1))`
        IF (NOT (`I perform work in an industry under it` OR `it is related or collateral to such a contract with work a significant purpose`))
            THEN `no: the order is for a contract whereby a person performs work in an industry, or a related condition or collateral arrangement where the work is a significant purpose of the arrangements (s 106(1), (2A))`
        IF `it is a contract of employment` AND `the reason is one for an unfair dismissal application`
            THEN `no: Division 2 does not apply where the contract of employment is said to be unfair for a reason for which an unfair dismissal application has been or could have been made under Part 6, or could have been but for s 83 (s 109A)`
        IF `it is a contract of employment` AND (`the package over 12 months` `remuneration package` `months the package covers` GREATER THAN `the cap`)
            THEN `no: no application can be made about a contract of employment whose remuneration package over the 12 months before the application (or the termination) exceeds the remuneration cap (s 108A(1))`
        IF `I am a partner and it is with my partners` AND (`profit share` GREATER THAN `the cap`)
            THEN `no: a partner cannot apply about a contract with the other partners if the partner's profit share over the 12 months before the application (or the termination) exceeds the cap (s 108A(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you may apply to the Commission in Court Session for an order declaring the contract wholly or partly void, or varying it (ss 106, 108)`
    WHERE
        `the cap` MEANS `the remuneration cap` `a regulation prescribes a cap` `the prescribed cap`

§§ `The time for applying (s 108B)`

GIVEN `the day of termination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 108B last day` `the day of termination` MEANS `the day of termination` `plus months` 12

DECLARE `Unfair contract time answer` IS ONE OF
    `no time limit: the Act fixes a time only for a contract that has been terminated (s 108B(1))`
    `in time: the application was made not later than 12 months after the termination of the contract (s 108B(1))`
    `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 12 months after the termination have not passed (s 108B(1))`
    `out of time, but within the further 3 months: the Commission may accept it only if you satisfy it that there are exceptional circumstances justifying the late application (s 108B(3))`
    `too late: more than 15 months after the termination, and the Commission has no jurisdiction to extend the time or accept the application (s 108B(2), (3))`

GIVEN `it has been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day of termination` IS A DATE, `it has been made` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day made` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Unfair contract time answer`
`the s 108B answer` `it has been terminated` `the day of termination` `it has been made` `the day made` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `it has been terminated`)
            THEN `no time limit: the Act fixes a time only for a contract that has been terminated (s 108B(1))`
        IF `made by the last day` `the day of termination` (`the s 108B last day` `the day of termination`) `the day` AND `it has been made`
            THEN `in time: the application was made not later than 12 months after the termination of the contract (s 108B(1))`
        IF `made by the last day` `the day of termination` (`the s 108B last day` `the day of termination`) `the day`
            THEN `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 12 months after the termination have not passed (s 108B(1))`
        IF `made by the last day` `the day of termination` ((`the s 108B last day` `the day of termination`) `plus months` 3) `the day`
            THEN `out of time, but within the further 3 months: the Commission may accept it only if you satisfy it that there are exceptional circumstances justifying the late application (s 108B(3))`
        OTHERWISE `too late: more than 15 months after the termination, and the Commission has no jurisdiction to extend the time or accept the application (s 108B(2), (3))`
    WHERE
        `the day` MEANS `the day considered` `it has been made` `the day made` `today`

§ `Chapter 5 Part 1: freedom from victimisation (ss 210, 213)`

-- s 210(1): the reasons the section protects, (a) to (k).
DECLARE `The reason alleged` IS ONE OF
    `I am or was a union member or official, or an elected representative of employees`
    `I do not belong to a union, or hold a certificate of conscientious objection`
    `I refused to engage in industrial action`
    `I exercised functions conferred under this Act`
    `I claimed a benefit I am entitled to under industrial relations legislation or an industrial instrument`
    `I informed someone of an alleged breach by an employer of industrial relations legislation or an industrial instrument`
    `I participated, or proposed to participate, in proceedings relating to an industrial matter`
    `I engaged, or proposed to engage, in public or political activity`
    `I informed someone of an alleged breach of the Protection of the Environment Operations Act 1997 by an employer`
    `I reported or gave evidence about a rail safety notifiable occurrence, the safety of rail, bus or ferry operations, or dangerous goods transport`
    `I complained that a workplace matter is unsafe or a risk to health, or exercised work health and safety consultation functions`
    `I assisted IPART or the Scheme Administrator under the Electricity Supply Act 1995`
    `another reason`

DECLARE `Victimisation answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are presumed to have been victimised because of the matter you allege, and the employer or organisation has not satisfied the Commission that it was not a substantial and operative cause; you may apply for orders under s 213 (s 210(2))`
    `no: the presumption is rebutted, because the employer or organisation satisfied the Commission that the matter you allege was not a substantial and operative cause of the detrimental action (s 210(2))`
    `no: public or political activity is protected unless it interferes with the performance of your duties, and yours does (s 210(1)(h))`
    `s 210 does not reach this: it protects an employee or prospective employee`
    `s 210 does not reach this: the reason you allege is not one of those s 210(1) lists`
    `this Act does not say: the s 210(2) presumption arises only where you suffered a detriment as a result of the employer's or organisation's action, and "victimise" is not defined`

GIVEN `employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `suffered a detriment from their action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason` IS A `The reason alleged`
      `the activity interferes with my duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they satisfied the Commission it was not a substantial and operative cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Victimisation answer`
`the s 210 answer` `employee or prospective employee` `suffered a detriment from their action` `the reason` `the activity interferes with my duties` `they satisfied the Commission it was not a substantial and operative cause` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `employee or prospective employee`)
            THEN `s 210 does not reach this: it protects an employee or prospective employee`
        IF `the reason` EQUALS `another reason`
            THEN `s 210 does not reach this: the reason you allege is not one of those s 210(1) lists`
        IF (`the reason` EQUALS `I engaged, or proposed to engage, in public or political activity`) AND `the activity interferes with my duties`
            THEN `no: public or political activity is protected unless it interferes with the performance of your duties, and yours does (s 210(1)(h))`
        IF (NOT `suffered a detriment from their action`)
            THEN `this Act does not say: the s 210(2) presumption arises only where you suffered a detriment as a result of the employer's or organisation's action, and "victimise" is not defined`
        IF `they satisfied the Commission it was not a substantial and operative cause`
            THEN `no: the presumption is rebutted, because the employer or organisation satisfied the Commission that the matter you allege was not a substantial and operative cause of the detrimental action (s 210(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you are presumed to have been victimised because of the matter you allege, and the employer or organisation has not satisfied the Commission that it was not a substantial and operative cause; you may apply for orders under s 213 (s 210(2))`

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 213 last day` `the day of the contravention` MEANS `the day of the contravention` `plus days` 21

DECLARE `Victimisation time answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the application was made within 21 days after the contravention (s 213(3))`
    `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 21 days after the contravention have not passed (s 213(3))`
    `out of time: more than 21 days after the contravention; the Commission may accept it only if it considers there is a sufficient reason, having regard to the reason for and length of the delay, the hardship to you or the other party, and the conduct complained of (s 213(4))`

GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE, `it has been made` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day made` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Victimisation time answer`
`the s 213 answer` `the day of the contravention` `it has been made` `the day made` `today` MEANS
    IF `made by the last day` `the day of the contravention` (`the s 213 last day` `the day of the contravention`) (`the day considered` `it has been made` `the day made` `today`)
    THEN IF `it has been made`
         THEN `in time: the application was made within 21 days after the contravention (s 213(3))`
         ELSE `still in time: you have not applied yet, and 21 days after the contravention have not passed (s 213(3))`
    ELSE `out of time: more than 21 days after the contravention; the Commission may accept it only if it considers there is a sufficient reason, having regard to the reason for and length of the delay, the hardship to you or the other party, and the conduct complained of (s 213(4))`

§ `Chapter 7 Part 2: recovery of remuneration and other amounts`

-- ss 364-368: the kinds of amount an industrial court may order an employer to pay.
DECLARE `Kind of amount` IS ONE OF
    `an amount payable under an industrial instrument, or long service leave or annual holiday pay under the Acts s 364(2) names`
    `an amount payable under my contract of employment, where an industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate for the work`
    `an amount payable under my contract of employment, where no industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate for the work`
    `pay for work whose rate no industrial instrument fixes for me, though one fixes it for others (or for my other work with the same employer)`
    `superannuation contributions an industrial instrument requires my employer to make`

DECLARE `Who applies` IS ONE OF
    `I apply myself`
    `an inspector, a Public Service agency employee or a union officer applies for me, with my written consent`
    `someone else applies for me without my written consent`

DECLARE `Recovery answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to pay the unpaid amount (s 365)`
    `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to pay the unpaid amount under your contract (s 366)`
    `yes, if the industrial court is satisfied that it is just and equitable for the employer to pay you for the work: it fixes an appropriate rate and may order payment (s 367)`
    `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to restore you, as far as practicable, to the position you would be in had the contributions been made, including paying the unpaid contributions and their earnings to the fund (s 368)`
    `no: s 366 applies only if an industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate or amount of remuneration for the work (s 366(2)); you may still sue for the money as a debt in another court`
    `no: someone else may apply for you only with your written consent, and only an inspector, a Public Service agency employee or an officer of an industrial organisation (s 369(1)(b))`
    `no: an application may be made only for money that became due within the 6 years immediately before it (s 369(3))`

-- s 369(3): the last day to apply for money that fell due on a day (fork F3: the sixth anniversary).
GIVEN `the day it fell due` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the s 369 last day` `the day it fell due` MEANS `the day it fell due` `plus months` 72

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of amount`
      `who applies` IS A `Who applies`
      `the day it fell due` IS A DATE
      `it has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day made` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
`the recovery answer` `the kind` `who applies` `the day it fell due` `it has been made` `the day made` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `who applies` EQUALS `someone else applies for me without my written consent`
            THEN `no: someone else may apply for you only with your written consent, and only an inspector, a Public Service agency employee or an officer of an industrial organisation (s 369(1)(b))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `an amount payable under my contract of employment, where no industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate for the work`
            THEN `no: s 366 applies only if an industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate or amount of remuneration for the work (s 366(2)); you may still sue for the money as a debt in another court`
        IF (NOT (`made by the last day` `the day it fell due` (`the s 369 last day` `the day it fell due`) (`the day considered` `it has been made` `the day made` `today`)))
            THEN `no: an application may be made only for money that became due within the 6 years immediately before it (s 369(3))`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the kind`
            WHEN `an amount payable under an industrial instrument, or long service leave or annual holiday pay under the Acts s 364(2) names` THEN `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to pay the unpaid amount (s 365)`
            WHEN `an amount payable under my contract of employment, where an industrial instrument fixes the minimum rate for the work` THEN `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to pay the unpaid amount under your contract (s 366)`
            WHEN `pay for work whose rate no industrial instrument fixes for me, though one fixes it for others (or for my other work with the same employer)` THEN `yes, if the industrial court is satisfied that it is just and equitable for the employer to pay you for the work: it fixes an appropriate rate and may order payment (s 367)`
            OTHERWISE `yes: an industrial court may order your employer to restore you, as far as practicable, to the position you would be in had the contributions been made, including paying the unpaid contributions and their earnings to the fund (s 368)`

§§ `Small claims (s 379)`

-- s 379(3): $10,000 per employee, or "some other amount" prescribed by the regulations (higher or lower; not
-- deposited, so the person may give it).
GIVEN `a regulation prescribes another amount` IS A BOOLEAN, `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the small claims maximum` `a regulation prescribes another amount` `the prescribed amount` MEANS
    IF `a regulation prescribes another amount` THEN `the prescribed amount` ELSE 10000

DECLARE `Small claims answer` IS ONE OF
    `the whole amount claimed is within the small claims maximum, so a small claims order may be for all of it (s 379(3))`
    `a small claims order for you can be at most` HAS `the most` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the amount claimed` IS A NUMBER, `a regulation prescribes another amount` IS A BOOLEAN, `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Small claims answer`
`the s 379 answer` `the amount claimed` `a regulation prescribes another amount` `the prescribed amount` MEANS
    IF `the amount claimed` AT MOST `the small claims maximum` `a regulation prescribes another amount` `the prescribed amount`
    THEN `the whole amount claimed is within the small claims maximum, so a small claims order may be for all of it (s 379(3))`
    ELSE `a small claims order for you can be at most` (`the small claims maximum` `a regulation prescribes another amount` `the prescribed amount`)
